gvO(){return"per week"},
gnz(){return"An active recovery week?"},
pt(a,b){return"You've been training about "+a+" days a week for roughly "+b+" weeks. A good moment for an active recovery week: working weights and sets down 30\u201350%, or cardio only. This is a recommendation, not medical advice."},
gpu(){return"Not now"},
gpv(){return"Got it"},
goW(){return"Save a backup?"},
goT(){return"Your data lives only on this device. If it is lost or storage fails, that history is gone. Share a copy now, or postpone for 28 days."},
goV(){return"Share"},
goU(){return"Later"},
go6(){return"Training rhythm"},
vJ(a){return"You train about "+a+" times a week on average."},
vI(a,b){return a+" trains about "+b+" times a week on average."},
gvz(){return"An easy rhythm"},
gvA(){return"A steady rhythm"},
gvy(){return"A dense rhythm"},
gvB(){return"Almost no days off"},
gvD(){return"Where this number comes from"},
gvN(){return"Average over the last four weeks. Days with strength work count; cardio-only days do not. This is not a goal and not a grade \u2014 just your current rhythm."},
gvM(){return"Active recovery week"},
gvL(){return"Not a pause \u2014 a week at half power: working weights and set counts down 30\u201350%. You can skip strength entirely and keep cardio or any other activity. Muscle recovers faster than joints, ligaments, and tendons \u2014 this week gives them time to catch up."},
gvE(){return"What this means"},
gvv(){return"There are enough rest days between sessions that fatigue does not stack. No need to plan active recovery yet \u2014 at this rhythm the body recovers on its own."},
gvw(){return"A steady rhythm you can live on for years. If the sessions are hard, take an active recovery week every few months \u2014 better early than after the weights stall."},
gvu(){return"Sessions sit close together, and fatigue builds quietly. An active recovery week every two or three months usually keeps progress better than grinding without a break."},
gvx(){return"Almost every day under load. That can work if sleep and food keep up. At this rhythm an active recovery week about once a month is ordinary care for joints and ligaments, not a cop-out."},
gvG(){return"This is the rhythm people keep for years."},
gvF(){return"You train often \u2014 a schedule like that does not happen by itself."},
gvH(){return"Looks like you found the body's secret mode."},
gvK(){return"Load already dropped recently \u2014 active recovery can count as done. Pick the pace back up."},
